306:**B2 — the supervisor is a fail-closed state machine (`exp35_supervisor_state.json`, schema v1).** Fields: campaign / H35 / cells sha / supervisor sha; the baseline (time of our first spawn, his step then, his log path + inode + size then); per chunk `planned → in_flight → runner_verified → gates_verified` (with the runner rc, the receipt sha, the gate results); the lane GPU and the reservation epoch; a permanent `stop_latch` {reason, time}. Writes are atomic (temp file + fsync + rename); a corrupt or inconsistent state refuses to run. Restart reconciliation: a chunk with a verified receipt but no `gates_verified` re-runs its gates (E1 / E2 / probe / guard) before anything else; a non-zero runner rc, an absent receipt, a failed verification, a final guard failure or an invalid probe sets the stop latch before any next spawn; a set latch is never cleared by the supervisor (only by the Planner, by hand, after reporting). His log: if its inode changes or its size shrinks → hard stop (no baseline reset).

